<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abbey of Saint Martial, Limoges</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">848–1791</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Abbey of Saint Martial was a Benedictine monastery in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limoges">Limoges</a>, founded in 848 around the tomb of Saint Martial, the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of the city. From the tenth to the twelfth century it was among the great abbeys of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, known for its library and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> of early polyphonic music; the chronicler Adémar of Chabannes worked there. The abbey was suppressed and demolished after the Revolution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abbey-of-saint-martial-limoges.jpg" alt="Abbey of Saint Martial, Limoges" width="320" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Fayen et Maurice Bouguereau · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint-Martial_sur_plan_de_Limoges.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
